course: dictionary
lesson: 4611
title: Hick: a rude word for country people
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can be rude even when it looks short and harmless. «Hick» is informal and rude in American English. It is used to insult someone from the countryside, as if they were simple and old-fashioned. Snobbish characters in American stories use it to look down on country people.
explain: The word has other meanings too. As an adjective, a hick town is a small, rural and old-fashioned town. Hick can also be a short sound, like a hiccup. To check which meaning fits, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: The rhyme «HICK-o-ry, DICK-o-ry, DOCK» begins with the same sounds as hick. Clap the beat: the strong beat falls on HICK, so the first part of hickory is a rhythm, not an insult. Look at the whole word before you decide what it means.
explain: Kindness matters with words like this. Calling someone a hick mocks them for where they live. Choose words that describe a place without making fun of the people who live there.
fact: «Hick» (US, informal, rude) is an insulting word for someone from the countryside.
fact: As an adjective, «hick» means small, rural and old-fashioned, as in «a hick town».
fact: «Hick» can also be a short sound, like a hiccup.
fact: Calling people a hick mocks them for where they live, so it can hurt their feelings.
fact: Useful phrases: «a hick town» and «country hick».
exercise: Snobbish characters in American films call country people «hicks». What does hick mean as an insult? | Someone who is very rich and famous | A tall tree in a forest | *Someone from the countryside, seen as simple and old-fashioned | A kind teacher
exercise: In the phrase «a hick town», what kind of word is hick? | A verb, meaning to run very fast | A noun for a type of fish | *An adjective, meaning small, rural and old-fashioned | A word for a loud shout
exercise: Hick can also be a sound. Which word means a similar sound? | Hum | Shout | *Hiccup | Whistle
test: Why is calling someone a hick unkind? | It is a kind compliment | It makes them richer | *It mocks them for where they live
test: In «HICK-o-ry, DICK-o-ry, DOCK», which word starts with the same sound as hick? | Clock | *Hickory | Mouse | Dock
exam: Which use of «hick» is rude and mocking? | Naming a hickory tree in the park | Saying a hick, the short sound you make with hiccups | Describing a small, quiet town as a hick town | *Calling someone a hick because they live in the countryside
